# name: test/sql/reference/null_distributions_reference.test
# description: #304 auc_null_quantile / auc_null_p_value and ptukey / qtukey vs base R
# group: [reference]
#
# Reference values: validation/generators/make_reference_null_distributions.R (base R):
#  * auc_null_quantile(p, m, n) = qwilcox(p, m, n) / (m n)
#  * auc_null_p_value(auc, m, n) = pwilcox(ceiling(auc m n) - 1, m, n, lower.tail = FALSE)
#  * beyond m n = 10000 the normal approximation (upstream's documented formula, in base R;
#    tolerance 1e-10: statrs' normal tail differs from R's pnorm by ~4e-12)
#  * ptukey / qtukey = R ptukey / qtukey (qtukey is R's secant iteration, eps 1e-4,
#    which upstream ports). Tolerances 1e-9 (ptukey) and 1e-7 (qtukey), as upstream's
#    own R validation: the integration agrees with R to ~1e-11, not to the last bit.
# p = 0 and p = 1 are exact boundaries, as qwilcox (anofox-statistics >= 0.8.1; 0.7.0
# returned 0.93 for auc_null_quantile(1, 50, 40)), also next to them (1e-12, 1 - 1e-12).

require anofox_statistics

statement ok
